// `#![derive(X)]` whose X no module in the `use` list claims. Refused as the module-level fact it
// is, before the generator program is loaded -- it said "the module generator for 'Nobody' failed:
// no such function" when the check fell through to the bundled lookup, which describes the
// compiler's search rather than the reader's mistake.
#![derive(Nobody)]

fn main() {
    print(1)
}
